# Commercial S4 server verifier argument omission

## Safe code

`S4_SERVER_VERIFIER_REPOSITORY_ROOT_REQUIRED`

## Result

After the exact stopped Control checkout advanced to `e3de23711b63343352d76edf2a0877c12729e74e`, the runtime-authorization parser check passed. The following read-only application verifier invocation omitted its mandatory `--repository-root` argument and exited with argparse status 2.

No installation, migration, unit change, contract activation or service start occurred. The corrective invocation is:

`python -m tu1nz_commercial_s3.verify --repository-root /opt/tu1nz_repos/adult-publishing-core`

The repository-root argument is a read-only path binding and does not change the release.
